    {"page": 50, "text": "Book page 108, right-hand table (2015 Today's Monarch through 2019 This is Canada!): the printed price column appears misaligned by one row — no price is printed on the Today's Monarch line and a value of 15.00 appears on the NOTE line. Prices transcribed by visual line alignment and all 12 rows flagged uncertain. If the column is shifted up by one row instead, the mapping would be: Today's Monarch 25.00, Birth Stone Collection (12)* 25.00, Superman Shield (1 oz) 35.00, Cougar (1 oz) 35.00, Proudly Canadian 10.00, Lynx (1 oz) 35.00, Birth Stone Series (12)* 25.00, Hearts Aglow 12.00, Wolf (1 oz) 35.00, Zodiac (12)* 25.00, Grizzly Bear (1 oz) 35.00, This is Canada! 15.00."},
    {"page": 51, "text": "Image page 51 is a duplicate (dark) scan of the same book pages 110-111 shown in image page 52 (light scan). Content transcribed once under page 52."},
    {"page": 52, "text": "Book pages 110-111, MONTREAL 1976 OLYMPIC GAMES: For the Summer Olympic Games of 1976 held in Montreal, seven series of silver coins were minted, four different coins in each series (two $5.00 and two $10.00), struck in sterling silver. The $5.00 coins weigh 24.3 grams and the $10.00 coins weigh 48.6 grams. Sets of four coins with a face value of $30.00 contain 4.28 oz. of fine silver. Coins were available encapsulated in plastic, as single coins, and in custom, prestige and proof four-coin sets."},
    {"page": 52, "text": "Montreal 1976 table has columns: Date | Series | $5 Coin | $10 Coin | Custom Set | Prestige Set | Proof Set. All column values are recorded in the description field of each row. Book note: A set equals 2 x $5.00 coins and 2 x $10.00 coins of the same year."},
    {"page": 53, "text": "Book pages 112-113. NOTE printed on book page 113: * Price per individual coin (applies to 2012-2023 Welcome to the World*)."},
    {"page": 54, "text": "Book pages 114-115. NOTE printed on book page 115: * Price per individual coin (applies to NHL Cdn. Teams (7)*)."},
    {"page": 55, "text": "Book pages 116-117. NOTE printed on both pages: * Price per individual coin."},
    {"page": 56, "text": "Book pages 118-119. Chinese Lunar Calendar Silver Commemoratives table appears under the 15 DOLLAR SILVER COMMEMORATIVES heading."}
